{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Your desires</b> — anything that you desire." "<b>They are comparable</b> — from the root of ולמלך אין שוה, and its meaning is that the people are worth nothing, and it is accounted to the king that he should disregard them, for they are a scattered and dispersed people, and despised."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:20:54.270044278Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}